      "writtenOn": "2024-04-08T19:08:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fine with either too. I have slight preference to have components, as it\u0027s a bit straight forward to use and less confusing, because we\u0027re actually swapping U and V, not R and B (i.e swap is _before_ the conversion), as long as it doesn\u0027t cause any problems with the pipeline keys. \n\nWe\u0027re talking about adding 1 bit (bool) vs... 12 (4 x 3 bits swizzle flags)? If using 1 bit is preferable, we can use bool, I don\u0027t expect any other weird swizzlings here.",
      "parentUuid": "221f6839_735eacb8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 80,
